 </span>\n\nThis session provides a factual overview of PLIDA as a national
  linked administrative data asset. It will cover the population base\, bro
 ad data domains\, modular structure\, longitudinal coverage\, major source
  datasets and the general logic of linkage.\n\nThis session examines the i
 nterpretation of administrative records for research and policy analysis. 
 It will focus on what administrative data can and cannot measure\, includi
 ng distinctions between service use and need\, eligibility and receipt\, d
 iagnosis and administrative classification\, treatment and payment records
 \, and socioeconomic circumstances and administrative proxies.\n\nThis ses
