 records available through PLIDA\, including MBS\, PBS and NDIS data. It wi
 ll cover module structure\, file organisation\, coding systems\, coverage
 \, timing\, documentation and common interpretation issues specific to the
 se records.\n\nThis session puts the preceding material into practice by w
 orking through examples of how research and policy questions can be transl
 ated into PLIDA analysis files. It will cover choices about study populati
 ons\, observation periods\, event records\, person-level summaries\, longi
 tudinal structure\, and documentation of key decisions. The session may in
 clude worked examples and project-based discussion to help participants th
 ink through how research questions can be implemented using PLIDA.\n\nThis
